      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T18:02:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not wait for LTS?  There should be no need to do anything special in Android for this fix.",
      "revId": "965516abb209e4105b88bc2bf13dd37996ba1e7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "484f9cae_21040c37",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1979492
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T20:29:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having the fix sooner in the relevant branches extends the testing period. It also spares me of the time spent tracking such bugs. I can extend your question as well: why do we use the UPSTREAM tag at all? Why don\u0027t we wait for the android-lts branch to be merged into its android correspondent branches?",
      "parentUuid": "f4341423_a17be94c",
      "revId": "965516abb209e4105b88bc2bf13dd37996ba1e7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "727f65d8_286621a4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T20:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The UPSTREAM tag exists primarily for patches that are wanted in Android but not LTS.  For example, new features.\n\nYou can submit this anyway, if you want to, but I think your time would be better spent working on bugs that have not already been fixed.  Not like there\u0027s a shortage of them: https://syzkaller.appspot.com",
      "parentUuid": "484f9cae_21040c37",
      "revId": "965516abb209e4105b88bc2bf13dd37996ba1e7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bfe6134b_acc3096f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1979492
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T20:57:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I rechecked the patch. Another (and maybe the strongest) reason why it\u0027s needed is that the blamed commit was introduced in v5.18 and it\u0027s not available in linux-stable/linux-5.15.y, but available in aosp/android13-5.15-lts. Thus the fix will never arrive in 5.15.y if no-one has an interest in backporting the blamed commit as well. And we would end up waiting indefinitely for the fix to get to android.\n\nAnd regarding the first arguments, I prefer closing the bugs than spending time tracking them, I find the later more time consuming. At least that\u0027s what I feel until now.",
      "parentUuid": "727f65d8_286621a4",
      "revId": "965516abb209e4105b88bc2bf13dd37996ba1e7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98062be0_2996b8d4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T21:06:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, I didn\u0027t realize that you were backporting this because it Fixes a commit that was backported to this kernel branch.  That\u0027s fine then.\n\nIn parallel I think I\u0027m still going to get this included in 5.10 and 5.15 LTS, as it applies to there too.  It was ambiguous what to put in the Fixes tag (see the commit message).",
      "parentUuid": "bfe6134b_acc3096f",
      "revId": "965516abb209e4105b88bc2bf13dd37996ba1e7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
